" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046465/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-275244" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $p=⟨2,1,-2⟩$ and $q=⟨3,2,0⟩.$ Find the exact value of the scalar projection of $p$ onto $q.$\n\n${\\text{comp}}_{q}\\,p=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046465/state.json" "file_sha256" "181d70ca55f6a30d3056a4fbec85eddc07d7b7e8cfb5fb3f5ecf1be648e81d12" "basis" 1685 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046465/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-275244" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the formula for the scalar projection, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{q}\\,p & =\\frac{p\\cdot q}{|\\,q\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{p}_{x}{q}_{x}+{p}_{y}{q}_{y}+{p}_{z}{q}_{z}}{\\sqrt{{q}_{x}^{2}+{q}_{y}^{2}+{q}_{z}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\cdot 3+1\\cdot 2+(-2)\\cdot 0}{\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{2}^{2}+{0}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{13}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046465/state.json" "file_sha256" "181d70ca55f6a30d3056a4fbec85eddc07d7b7e8cfb5fb3f5ecf1be648e81d12" "basis" 1685 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046465/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-275244" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046465/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "116abfe154838a6164d2dc5466f4720d03ebc4992780a9c9dbe8b22a380f4e02" "basis" 1685 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046465/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-275244" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046465/state.json" "file_sha256" "181d70ca55f6a30d3056a4fbec85eddc07d7b7e8cfb5fb3f5ecf1be648e81d12" "basis" 1685 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046465/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-275244" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{13}}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046465/state.json" "file_sha256" "181d70ca55f6a30d3056a4fbec85eddc07d7b7e8cfb5fb3f5ecf1be648e81d12" "basis" 1685 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046465/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-275256" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $a=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]$ and $b=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ x \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$ Given that the scalar projection of $a$ onto $b$ is $0,$ find the value of $x.$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046465/state.json" "file_sha256" "181d70ca55f6a30d3056a4fbec85eddc07d7b7e8cfb5fb3f5ecf1be648e81d12" "basis" 1685 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046465/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-275256" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since $p$ is a nonzero vector, its scalar projection onto another nonzero vector $q$ equals zero only when the vectors are perpendicular. \n\nSo, we must have\n\n$$\np⊥q\\,⟹\\,p\\cdot q=0.\n$$\n\nComputing the dot product, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot q & ={p}_{x}\\cdot {q}_{x}+{p}_{y}\\cdot {q}_{y}+{p}_{z}\\cdot {q}_{z} \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot 0+2\\cdot x+4\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =2x+8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot q & =0 \\\\ 2x+8 & =0 \\\\ 2x & =-8 \\\\ x & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046465/state.json" "file_sha256" "181d70ca55f6a30d3056a4fbec85eddc07d7b7e8cfb5fb3f5ecf1be648e81d12" "basis" 1685 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046465/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-275256" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046465/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "116abfe154838a6164d2dc5466f4720d03ebc4992780a9c9dbe8b22a380f4e02" "basis" 1685 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046465/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-275256" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046465/state.json" "file_sha256" "181d70ca55f6a30d3056a4fbec85eddc07d7b7e8cfb5fb3f5ecf1be648e81d12" "basis" 1685 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046465/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-275256" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-4"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046465/state.json" "file_sha256" "181d70ca55f6a30d3056a4fbec85eddc07d7b7e8cfb5fb3f5ecf1be648e81d12" "basis" 1685 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046465/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-18374" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $p=⟨\\sqrt{2},1,-1⟩$ and $q=⟨\\sqrt{8},-\\sqrt{3},1⟩.$ Find the scalar projection of $p$ onto $q.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14061012/state.json" "file_sha256" "c0bd64da52539ae9a767050c98e9f91a69037b8f6835a6c9b464c504533ef368"} {"question" "q-18374" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the formula for the scalar projection, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{q}\\,p & =\\frac{p\\cdot q}{|\\,q\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{p}_{x}{q}_{x}+{p}_{y}{q}_{y}+{p}_{z}{q}_{z}}{\\sqrt{{q}_{x}^{2}+{q}_{y}^{2}+{q}_{z}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{8}+1\\cdot (-\\sqrt{3})+(-1)\\cdot 1}{\\sqrt{(\\sqrt{8})^{2}+(-\\sqrt{3})^{2}+{1}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3-\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{12}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3-\\sqrt{3}}{2\\sqrt{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}-1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14061012/state.json" "file_sha256" "c0bd64da52539ae9a767050c98e9f91a69037b8f6835a6c9b464c504533ef368"} {"question" "q-18374" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14061012/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d0615a346086edb0e1956bf5c50ff0d4cf1f6e1f77d01d718f95136c1c710a8b"} {"question" "q-18374" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/De